1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Hello everyone, today I will show you how to make a four-core buckle.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,000
First of all, the four-core buckle is divided into a combined state and an open state.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Here we will first explain the four-core buckle in a combined state.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Let's take the front door handle as an example.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
You can see that the corresponding board also has a four-core buckle.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:35,000
First of all, we use the hook and loop tool to hook the circle of the buckle into the inner line or shape.

7
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Then use the sewing tool to sew them together.

8
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Open the simulation.

9
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:52,000
In this way, we can simulate a four-core buckle in a combined state.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Next, we see the surface of the door handle.

11
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:02,000
If our four-core buckle does not have a face buckle, we need to hide the trace of the sewing line.

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Here we can use the editor sewing line tool to select the sewing line just added and change its hair line strength to 0.

13
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,000
In this way, we have a four-core buckle without a face buckle.

14
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:24,000
If we have a face buckle, we need to use the add button tool to add a button to the door handle.

15
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:34,000
In the right side of the door handle, we select the added button to modify its shape, size and material.

16
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Its color, surface light intensity, reflection intensity, etc. can be modified.

17
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Next, let's rotate the view.

18
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:51,000
You can see that there is still a gap between the button and the clothing fabric.

19
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Here we use the select button.

20
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,000
In this way, we can use the select move button tool.

21
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Select this button in front of us.

22
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Then, in the right side of the door handle, change the length of the line to a negative value.

23
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Let our button stick to our fabric.

24
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,000
At the same time, we also need to close the gap between the button and the fabric of the door handle in the door handle.

25
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:18,000
To avoid a conflict between the button and the fabric when we simulate.

26
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
This is our door handle.

27
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:26,000
This is how we make a four-box button in the collection state.

28
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Next, let's see how the four-box button works.

29
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,000
The face button is still the same method.

30
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:39,000
If there is no face button, we can skip this step.

31
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Next, let's add the purple button and the mother button.

32
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:47,000
You can see that the purple button should be added on the reverse side of the door handle.

33
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
The mother button is on the collar.

34
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,000
We find the body window.

35
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:57,000
In the button button column, click on the add two default buttons.

36
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Then, name them separately as the purple button and the mother button.

37
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Next, we choose the purple button.

38
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Use the add button tool to add it to our door handle.

39
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,000
The position of our face button is the same.

40
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Next, we switch the tool to the select move button tool.

41
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Select the two buttons that we just added.

42
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Then, click on the right button to find the flip button.

43
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Flip them to the reverse side of our fabric.

44
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Then, in the body window, we select the current purple button.

45
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:39,000
To modify their shape, size and material.

46
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
In the same way, let's make the mother button.

47
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Next, we use the top button to adjust its height.

48
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Finally, let's get the button button to adjust the length of the button.

49
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Let them stick to the surface of our fabric.

50
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Turn off the conflict of button button.

51
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:15,000
To prevent a conflict of button button in the later simulation.

52
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Continue to increase the perspective of the button button.

53
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:24,000
This is the production method of our four-core code.

